A thread taken off a ring while it is the oldest stays the ring's head.
The next signal would wake a thread that is no longer waiting,
and the next switch run one that is already running;
a queue holds only threads in the state it is for.

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -45,5 +45,2 @@ static void ring_remove(paddr_t *head, struct thread *t)
         ((struct thread *)p2v(t->queue_next))->queue_prev = t->queue_prev;
-        if (*head == v2p(t)) {
-            *head = t->queue_next;
-        }
     }
